WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.100
A rat was traveling along the king's highway.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:10.180
He was a very proud rat considering his small size and the bad reputation all rats have.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.580
As Mr.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.240
Rat walked along, he kept mostly to the ditch.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.240
He noticed a great commotion up the road, and soon a grand procession came in view.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.520
It was the king and his retinue.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.100
The king rode on a huge elephant adorned with the most gorgeous trappings.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.460
With the king and his luxurious howda were the royal dog and cat.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.740
A great crowd of people followed the procession.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.800
They were so taken up with admiration of the elephant that the rat was not noticed.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.780
His pride was hurt.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.420
What fools, he cried.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.040
Look at me, and you will soon forget that clumsy elephant.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:55.140
Is it his great size that makes your eyes pop out, or is it his wrinkled hide?

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.980
Why, I have eyes and ears, and as many legs as he.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:06.060
I am of just as much importance, and but just then the royal cat spied him.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.900
And the next instant the rat knew he was not quite so important as an elephant.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.300
A resemblance to the great in some things does not make us great.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.280
The boys and the frogs.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:26.460
Some boys were playing one day at the edge of a pond, in which lived a family of frogs.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:33.640
The boys amused themselves by throwing stones into the pond so as to make them skip on top of the water.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:43.320
The stones were flying thick and fast, and the boys were enjoying themselves very much, but the poor frogs in the pond were trembling with fear.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:58.460
At last one of the frogs, the oldest and bravest, put his head out of the water and said, oh please dear children, stop your cruel play, though it may be fun for you, it means death to us.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.040
Always stop to think whether your fun may not be the cause of another's unhappiness.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.880
The crow and the pitcher.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:15.900
In a spell of dry weather, when the birds could find very little to drink, a thirsty crow found a pitcher with a little water in it.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:22.760
But the pitcher was high and had a narrow neck, and no matter how he tried the crow could not reach the water.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.100
The poor thing felt as if he must die of thirst.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.040
Then an idea came to him.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:34.340
Picking up some small pebbles, he dropped them into the pitcher one by one.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:41.260
With each pebble the water rose a little higher until at last it was near enough so he could drink.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.980
In a pinch a good use of our wits may help us out.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.120
The ants and the grasshopper.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:59.800
One bright day in late autumn a family of ants were bustling about in the warm sunshine, drying out the grain they had stored up during the summer.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:07.200
When a starving grasshopper, his fiddle under his arm, came up and humbly begged for a bite to eat.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:08.480
What?

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.040
cried the ants in surprise.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.800
Haven't you stored anything away for the winter?

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.820
What in the world were you doing all last summer?

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.040
I didn't have time to store up any food wine the grasshopper.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.140
I was so busy making music that before I knew it the summer was gone.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.980
The ants shrugged their shoulders and discussed.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.920
Making music were you, they cried.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.040
Very well.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:31.880
Now dance.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.160
And they turned their backs on the grasshopper and went on with their work.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.180
There's a time for work and a time for play.
